metalive <publicREMOVE@THISmetalive.net> wrote:
>Hail!
>
>What is the ring of conflict good for? OK, all I know is that monsters 
>sometimes will attack each other,

That is pretty damned useful, really.  If they're attacking each other,
they aren't attacking *you*.  Also, monsters that swallow their targets
instantly kill other monsters if their swallow attack hits.

>but also, my pet could kill me.

It could. This requires some caution on your part.

>So is it only safe to wear the ring after my pet has died

As long as *you* aren't next to your pet, and something else *is*, your
pet remains quite likely to go after the monsters instead of you.

It is more important to avoid wearing a ring of conflict while in the
vicinity of powerful peaceful monsters like shopkeepers, temple priests,
and the Minetown watch.  Also, don't wear it when you don't need it, as
it greatly increases your metabolic rate.

>(which usually 
>happens quite soon in this insanely difficult and unfair game, as it 
>never survived more than a few levels (nor have I)).

Nethack is not unfair (at least, not very often), but it is very difficult.
You have to pay attention to what is happening.  You may find it
profitable to read spoilers such as those maintained by Dylan O'Donnell.

>What is the pet 
>good for anyway, apart from biting or killing a few monsters sometimes. 
>How do I teach it useful things?

Throwing a treat (apples for herbivores, tripe or meatballs for
carnivores, and there may be other cases I've missed) at your pet just
after it has dropped something next to you greatly increases its
"apport", which determines how likely it is to drop things next to you.
Shopkeepers do not care about pets picking up items and removing them
from the shop.  The tactic here is reasonably obvious, I think :)
